  - chromatic-choosability
  - critical graph
  - odd hole
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  We prove the complete Fiujlaali-McDonald conjecture on odd antiholes
  unconditionally: for every l >= 3 the only assignments of (l-1)-element
  lists from which the odd antihole on 2l-1 vertices cannot be coloured are
  the constant ones. Consequently, an odd-hole-free k-critical graph of
  maximum degree D containing an odd antihole of length 2(D-k)+7 is that
  antihole. The main theorem is checked in the Lean 4 kernel.
